WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.001
The second Kahn-Kalai conjecture.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.029
When does a random graph first contain H?

3
00:00:05.029 --> 00:00:06.980
The culprit: a rare piece of H.

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.035
Nested pieces share one random graph, so

5
00:00:11.035 --> 00:00:13.270
the log cost is paid only once.

6
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.115
Claimed: right up to a log factor.

7
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:18.916
Main theorem in Lean.
